#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This course is based on a live course held at the University of Tokyo in "
"2024, full of utility scale examples."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Welcome to utility-scale quantum computing!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This course is based on a live course held at the University of Tokyo in "
"2024. Each lesson consists of a PDF that was used in a lecture context, and "
"a computational lab activity. In some cases, the labs are sparse and merely "
"show a workflow and the explanation is in the associated PDF. In other "
"cases, the labs contain detailed explanations and mathematical motivation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Lessons 2-6** cover famous algorithms like Grover's and quantum phase "
"estimation. These are undeniably important to our understanding of the "
"potential power of quantum computing, but they are mostly tangential to the "
"utility-scale calculation to which we are building. If you are new to "
"quantum computing, you should definitely work through these. If you have "
"substantial experience in quantum computing, nothing new is added in these "
"lessons that is specific to the utility-scale calculation at hand.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Lessons 7-8** review quantum and classical simulation. The lesson on "
"classical simulation was written by Professor Yoshiaki Kawase of the "
"University of Tokyo, and is hosted externally on GitHub.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Lesson 9** focuses on modern quantum computing hardware.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Beginning in **lesson 10**, we cover topics that are of special importance "
"in the context of a utility-scale calculation. Understanding circuit "
"optimization (**lesson 10**) and mitigation of errors (**lesson 11**) is "
"critical to achieving good results at this scale. The utility-scale "
"calculation itself begins in **lesson 12** and concludes in **lesson 14**.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Good-faith estimates of required QPU time have been provided at the top of "
"each lesson, but your calculations might vary slightly. There is no quiz or "
"badge associated with this course.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We hope these instructional assets are useful to you and your students in "
"achieving useful quantum computing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Download the "
"pdf](https://ibm.ent.box.com/public/static/pnb9vhw1ruz72r3wp4pwfilwc7rzmufw.zip)"
" of the introductory lecture. Note that throughout all pdfs some code "
"snippets might become deprecated since these are static images.\n"
msgstr ""
